event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":104,"item_id":"rs_0e7522f841c67583016aca1bb0aa2c81949a7d59ae3aebf2bf","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Exploring server-side rendering forms**\n\nI’m thinking about implementing server-side rendering (SSR) for forms that are accessible and don’t require JavaScript. I need to focus on the HTML/CSS/JS stack while keeping it functional. If I create a blank form, it should alert on a POST response, showing an unchanged status (400), and for valid submissions, it should redirect with a status (303). I’ll also consider buttons, forms, and action methods. There’s plenty of time to test and refine my approach."}

event: response.reasoning_summary_part.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_part.done","sequence_number":105,"item_id":"rs_0e7522f841c67583016aca1bb0aa2c81949a7d59ae3aebf2bf","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"part":{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Exploring server-side rendering forms**\n\nI’m thinking about implementing server-side rendering (SSR) for forms that are accessible and don’t require JavaScript. I need to focus on the HTML/CSS/JS stack while keeping it functional. If I create a blank form, it should alert on a POST response, showing an unchanged status (400), and for valid submissions, it should redirect with a status (303). I’ll also consider buttons, forms, and action methods. There’s plenty of time to test and refine my approach."}}

